# Line-ending policy for a kit developed on macOS, Linux AND Windows.
#
# Everything in this repo is consumed by POSIX tooling: bash sources the engine,
# CMake reads the presets, Python reads config.json.in. A CRLF committed from a
# Windows clone breaks the other two platforms immediately and unhelpfully --
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` fails with "bad interpreter: ...^M", and a shell `case`
# arm gains an invisible \r that never matches.
#
# eol=lf (not merely text=auto) also makes Windows CHECK OUT LF, so a Windows
# working tree matches the index and `git status` stays meaningful there.
#
# NOTE: this governs files as they are committed and checked out from here on.
# A working tree that already holds CRLF keeps it until re-checked-out; to
# normalize an existing clone in place:
#
#     git add --renormalize .        # then review, then commit
#
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the file types where a stray CR is fatal rather than ugly.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.cmake text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.in    text eol=lf
*.tsv   text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts, if any are ever added, genuinely want CRLF.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

# Never munge binaries.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
